{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/140574-sidereals-and-charm-based-authority-over-other-exalted","id":140574,"title":"Sidereals and Charm-based authority over other Exalted","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-17T08:45:24-07:00","id":140574,"title":"Sidereals and Charm-based authority over other Exalted","content":"<b>Note: I have no copy of the 2nd Edition Sidereal manual, so I'm speaking from knowledge of the 1st Edition version and the assurance that not much really changed.</b><br /> <br /> <br /> As Exalted and as Agents of Fate and Heaven, Sidereals have authority over the gods and elementals of the Perfected Celestial Hierarchy.<br /> <br /> Not only is this authority political, it is expressed in their Charms. Many Charms outside of Sidereal Occult grant a Vizier some focused and powerful influence over gods and elementals of a particular elemental aspect. (Salt into Ash Sleight, Sky Spirit Demand, Ice and Fire Binding, Song of Spirit Persuasion, Water and Fire Legion, Embracing Life Method, and Earth and Sky Bargain.)<br /> <br /> Elemental Vision is much the same, but for some reason is unique in extending its effects towards Terrestrial Exalted. Granted, the effect is reduced, but should it exist at all? If you dropped the clause such that the Charm only works on spirits, it's still a good Charm.<br /> <br /> <br /> Likewise, I wonder why 'Subordinate Inspiration Practice' should affect other Sidereals the same as spirits. It's not even a reduced effect like with Elemental Vision. Yet as with Elemental Vision, one could drop the Exalted-specific clause and still have a worthwhile Charm.<br /> <br /> <br /> Of course, I have long been enraged with 'Adopting the Untamed Face' and 'Dreaming the Wild Lands'. If Sidereals could specifically affect Lunars &quot;because it's wilderness magic and they're basically animals&quot;, why could they not specifically affect Solars with Bureacracy-based &quot;civilization magic&quot;?<br /> <br /> But currently, I'm also <i>outright puzzled</i>. Because animal gods are a thing, as are elementals no more intelligent than animals.<br /> <br /> Given how important dealing with gods is for Sidereals, why don't these Charms affect animal spirits at all? If Sidereals can exert power over gods through an elemental connection, surely they can use an animal connection. This would especially helpful in that there should be far many more than 300 gods related to animals, and the Sidereal is much more likely to meet scads of them than ever run across a Lunar Exalt face-to-face. (Doubly so since Sidereals will usually try to avoid proximity to Lunar Exalted as much as possible.)<br /> <br /> <br /> One could argue that Sidereal Exalted have no specific Solar-related influence-effects because the Solars are rightfully their superiors in the hierarchy... but that doesn't explain why they can exert authority over <i>equals</i>, such as other Sidereal Exalted (a neophyte could use SIP against Chejop Kejak as easily as the reverse) or the Lunar Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 05-17-2014, 11:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T12:06:37-07:00","id":140791,"title":"","content":"I have a copy of the 2e Sidereals Manual, the Errata, and time enough for investigation. Long story short, there doesn't appear to have been so much of that in 2nd edition, especially post-Errata. Here are my findings:<br /> <br /> - Subordinate Inspiration Technique doesn't appear to call out Sidereals as applicable targets; it seems to impact them as much as anyone. That said, its prerequisite (with which it seems it must be used?) does put the user outside Fate, which is especially impactful on Sidereals. This Charm doesn't seem to be about calling them out, though.<br /> <br /> - Elemental Vision does indeed still impact Dragon-Blooded, and Errata does <i>not</i> <i>technically</i> remove them from the list. The Errata's wording does, however, seem to shift the focus away from &quot;appropriate elementals and gods ... [and] Dragon-Blooded of the appropriate element&quot; and more to &quot;those strongly associated with relevant elements.&quot; That still seems like it encompasses Terrestrials of the appropriate element, while encompassing a great deal else.<br /> <br /> - Adopting the Untamed Face doesn't mention Lunars as applicable targets. Errata even spells out its only against entities of animal intelligence, which is great, as that both definitively rules out Lunars as targets <i>and</i> expands what the Charm can affect.<br /> <br /> - As a fun fact, the pre-Errata'd Becoming the Wilderness <i>does</i> mention Lunars who consider an area their home, as well as local spirits, as potential targets of more potent social attacks (so maybe part of Adopting the Untamed Face wound up there?). So, while &quot;Lunars are just animals&quot; can still be irksome, it at least manages some more consistency. Again, also kind of irrelevant, because Errata replaces the text of the Charm entirely. It's now more of a Charm for more easily surviving the wilderness, with no social effects or mention of Lunars at all.<br /> <br /> - Unweaving Method, post-Errata, cannot target creatures of death and calls out Abyssals as such.<br /> <br /> - Conclusive Wisdom also does not affect Abyssal Exalted or the dead. This makes sense, as the Charm is all about showing a vision of the target's impending death and, well. Been there, done that.<br /> <br /> In summary, it looks to be down to only Dragon-Blooded kinda called out, and two cases of Charms not working on Abyssals. There didn't appear to be any other mentions of particular Exalts in the Sidereal set (Errata or pre-Errata). In full disclosure, there <i>could</i> be Charms in there that specially affect other Sidereals, I was using Ctrl+F as the engine of my search and that was obviously not going to work efficiently for &quot;Sidereal&quot; references in their own Charm section. Anyone better versed can speak up on the situation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T14:08:57-07:00","id":140926,"title":"","content":"Exalted are meant to be outside of the Celestial hierarchy (even Sidereals are to an extent -- they're like special agents, people who have a connection to the government but are outside of it enough to do things that normal agents couldn't do.) It doesn't make sense for the Sidereal charms that interact with gods via that thematic to treat the Exalted the same way.<br /> <br /> When their charms do affect the Exalted, it is more likely to be through their thematics as manipulative advisers or fate-ninjas, rather than any authority derived from the Celestial hierarchy, because the Celestial hierarchy doesn't give anyone authority over Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T14:32:38-07:00","id":140939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/140574-sidereals-and-charm-based-authority-over-other-exalted?p=140791#post140791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a copy of the 2e Sidereals Manual, the Errata, and time enough for investigation. Long story short, there doesn't appear to have been so much of that in 2nd edition, especially post-Errata.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's embarrassing that I didn't think to check the errata, first.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - As a fun fact, the pre-Errata'd Becoming the Wilderness <i>does</i> mention Lunars who consider an area their home, as well as local spirits, as potential targets of more potent social attacks (so maybe part of Adopting the Untamed Face wound up there?). So, while &quot;Lunars are just animals&quot; can still be irksome, it at least manages some more consistency. Again, also kind of irrelevant, because Errata replaces the text of the Charm entirely. It's now more of a Charm for more easily surviving the wilderness, with no social effects or mention of Lunars at all. </div> </div> </div>First Edition's 'Becoming the Wilderness' had nothing to do with Lunars. It was their target-number reducer for Survival and Awareness rolls in the wilderness.<br /> <br /> Did you mean to say 'Dreaming the Wild Lands'? The errata on DtWL does <i>not </i>say &quot;replace the text with the following&quot;. The errata on DtWL applies only to the environmental reshaping effect, not to any effect it has on Lunars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T15:07:06-07:00","id":140953,"title":"","content":"You have to try to figure out what the powers are there for, especially if you're proposing changes. Of course we can only speculate, but it seems really unlikely, in light of the overall Sidereal charmset and the structure of the book overall, that these powers were meant to convey Sidereal authority over the beings named. I kinda doubt it's just as simple as &quot;this magic also affects Lunars because they're basically animals,&quot; either, but, well, the point is that if you don't have a strong sense of why these powers are included then trying to extrapolate logically about what other powers they imply Sidereals <i>should</i> have is unwise.<br /> <br /> My conjecture: A lot of sidereal charmsets are focused toolsets for the kind of tasks you are likely to be performing if you have a high rating and several charms in that Ability, rather than things specifically wired into the explicit mechanical function of that ability. Bureaucracy has powers that are likely to be useful if you're playing The Laundry or the Bourne Identity, Socialize has powers that are useful if you're playing a social intrigue drama, Sail has powers that are likely to be useful if you're going on dramatic ocean voyages, and so on. This doesn't apply to every Sidereal charm, especially in the combat abilities, but it's a good rule of thumb for analyzing Sidereal powers in general: their charmtrees strongly encourage you to be in the thematic context associated with the linked Ability.<br /> <br /> So if I take this understanding and apply it to the Survival tree: this tree is about venturing into the depths of the untamed wilderness, the thematic heartland of the Survival ability. A Sidereal with a bunch of Survival charms is going to find themselves doing so often -- OOCly it's because the GM will want to give them opportunities to use that ability,and ICly it's because Sidereals tend to be assigned to roles they're suited for. The tree gives you tools to deal with the various hazards you are likely to encounter in that context, and that includes &quot;Lunar Exalted will try to kill you&quot;, because this is 1e and Lunars are Garou who love wilderness and hate civilization. As a Sidereal, you <i>would</i> like to avoid dealing with Lunars, but if you're Survival-focused, you don't really get a choice, so you have tools to help you out on that front. There's really no Ability-venue that introduces a similarly high chance of having issues with Solars -- the closest thing is Martial Arts, which didn't even have a native tree in 1e.<br /> <br /> For what it's worth: Adopting the Untamed Face is fine; it's a negligible social bonus in a game with no social mechanics. Dreaming the Wild Lands is kinda dumb, though -- it seems to be written under the assumption that Lunars are always minor NPCs. In both cases it's very clearly a matter of Survival bringing you into communion with the spirit of the wilderness, and thereby becoming appealing to Lunars since they share that quality, rather than &quot;this works on animals so it should probably also work on Lunars&quot;. I don't really know what's up with Elemental Vision, honestly, beyond &quot;Sidereals spend a lot of time managing DBs so here's a low-hanging power that helps with that.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 05-17-2014, 06:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T16:33:27-07:00","id":141012,"title":"","content":"EDIT: Smart Gayo is smart.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/140574-sidereals-and-charm-based-authority-over-other-exalted?p=140939#post140939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's embarrassing that I didn't think to check the errata, first.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, everyone's got their off moments. I wouldn't worry.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> First Edition's 'Becoming the Wilderness' had nothing to do with Lunars. It was their target-number reducer for Survival and Awareness rolls in the wilderness.<br /> <br /> Did you mean to say 'Dreaming the Wild Lands'? The errata on DtWL does <i>not </i>say &quot;replace the text with the following&quot;. The errata on DtWL applies only to the environmental reshaping effect, not to any effect it has on Lunars. </div> </div> </div>Just double-checked and I can confirm I was correct in what I said. Second Edition's &quot;Dreaming the Wild Lands&quot; <i>is</i> an environmental reshaping effect. Pre- and post-Errata versions don't mention Lunars at all.<br /> <br /> Perhaps the social part of 1e DtWL that mentioned Lunars was shuffled into 2e's pre-Errata BtW? The gist of it was mostly &quot;get ignored by and subtly influence animals, and can always channel Valor in social dealings with local spirits or Lunars who consider it home.&quot; 2e's post-Errata BtW is completely different, and sounds like it's closer in spirit to 1e's BtW.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":". 05-17-2014, 07:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}